@*
    The Goals view (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#the-goals-view), drawn from a
    GoalsBoardModel with every act a callback, so the storybook draws it with no module
    behind it and the host turns each callback into its own call.

    The header holds the title, the iteration switch — Day, Week, 2 weeks, Month — the
    last and next window as "12–16 Oct → 19–23 Oct", New goal, an icon-only Copy that
    puts the four stand-up blocks on the clipboard as plain text, and Refresh.

    Under GOALS, its heading carrying the count as the stand-up's blocks do, each goal is a GoalCard; one is open at a time, the first when the view
    first draws. Below the goals, No goal lists the work in progress in scope that no
    goal holds, each with Attach…: with a goal open it attaches to that goal, titled
    "Attach to ‹goal›"; with none open it hands the work to OnPickGoal, and the host
    opens the shared GoalPicker for it. Every item is a GoalSubject, handed back as it
    came; the board never reads one. A search beside the No goal heading filters its rows
    as it is typed, by the attach search's rule (GoalCard.IsMatch): title, number, a
    leading + or # tolerated. A query that hides every row says No matches; clearing it
    shows them all. The query is the board's own and never reaches the host.

    The open goal is edited in place, its rows detached and the goal deleted through
    GoalCard; each act reaches the host only when it listens (OnEditGoal, OnDetach,
    OnDeleteGoal, and OnQuickAddTask for the open goal's "New task" row, with the goal and
    the title typed). Delete goal… asks first in a destructive ConfirmDialog that says what
    the goal held stays as it is, and the goal is folded before the host is told.

    The goals are in the person's order. With a host listening on OnMoveGoal, each goal can
    be dragged by its grip — the library's one pointer reorder in components.js
    (backlogListReorder), registered under the goals column's data-list-owner, since a
    native drag is aborted in the desktop head's WebView2 — or moved one place with Move up
    and Move down. A held goal is drawn in the place of the goal it is over, and a drop puts
    it there. Passing over the held goal itself, or a gap between goals, keeps the last
    target; a drag that never reached another goal, or Escape, moves nothing. The new order is drawn at once and
    said in a live region ("Moved ‹goal› to position n of m."), and the move reaches the host
    as the goal and its new place; the next model the host hands in replaces the order
    drawn, which is how a refused move puts the stored order back.

    Beside the goals sits the StandUpPanel aside, which falls under them in one column
    once the board is narrower than 900 px. With no goals and nothing in progress
    outside one, the goals column is a real empty state with New goal as its action.
*@
@inject IJSRuntime Js
@implements IAsyncDisposable
<div class="@ClassValue" data-testid="@TestId">
    <header class="goals-board__header">
        <h1 class="goals-board__title">Goals</h1>
        <RadioGroup TValue="GoalsIteration"
                    Options="Iterations"
                    Value="Model.Iteration"
                    ValueChanged="length => IterationChanged.InvokeAsync(length)"
                    OptionLabel="GoalsText.Iteration"
                    OptionTestId="@(length => Part($"iteration-{length.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()}"))"
                    AriaLabel="Iteration"
                    Disabled="Busy"
                    CssClass="goals-board__iteration"
                    TestId="@Part("iteration")" />
        <span class="goals-board__window" data-testid="@Part("window")">@GoalsText.Window(Model.Last, Model.Next)</span>
        <span class="goals-board__spacer" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <AppButton OnClick="() => OnNewGoal.InvokeAsync()" TestId="@Part("new-goal")" id="@_newGoalId">New goal</AppButton>
        <CopyButton Text="@StandUpClipboard.Text(Model)"
                    Label="Copy"
                    StatusCssClass="sr-only"
                    TestId="@Part("copy")"
                    ButtonTestId="@Part("copy-button")"
                    StatusTestId="@Part("copy-status")" />
        <IconButton AriaLabel="Refresh" Title="Refresh" Disabled="Busy" OnClick="() => OnRefresh.InvokeAsync()" TestId="@Part("refresh")">
            <RefreshCwIcon />
        </IconButton>
    </header>

    <Alert Message="@Error" TestId="@Part("error")" />

    @if (CanMoveGoals)
    {
        <p class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-testid="@Part("move-announcement")">@_moveAnnouncement</p>
    }

    <div class="goals-board__layout">
        <div class="goals-board__goals" data-testid="@Part("goals")" data-list-owner="@(CanMoveGoals ? _id : null)">
            <SectionHeader Title="Goals" Level="2" CssClass="goals-board__section-header">
                <Actions>
                    <Badge Kind="tone" Slug="quiet" TestId="@Part("goals-count")">@Model.Goals.Count</Badge>
                </Actions>
            </SectionHeader>

            @if (IsEmpty)
            {
                <EmptyState Title="No goals yet"
                            Description="Set a goal for what the work should land, then attach the plans, tasks and pull requests that count towards it."
                            TestId="@EmptyTestId">
                    <Icon><TargetIcon Size="20" /></Icon>
                    <Action>
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Primary" OnClick="() => OnNewGoal.InvokeAsync()" TestId="@Part("empty-new-goal")">New goal</AppButton>
                    </Action>
                </EmptyState>
            }
            else
            {
                var shown = Shown;
                for (var index = 0; index < shown.Count; index++)
                {
                    var goal = shown[index];
                    var place = index;
                    <GoalCard @key="goal.Id"
                              OnMove="@(CanMoveGoals ? EventCallback.Factory.Create<int>(this, delta => MoveByAsync(goal.Id, delta)) : default)"
                              CanMoveUp="@(place > 0)"
                              CanMoveDown="@(place < shown.Count - 1)"
                              Dragging="@(goal.Id == _dragging)"
                              Goal="goal"
                              Expanded="@(goal.Id == _selected)"
                              OnToggle="() => ToggleAsync(goal.Id)"
                              Candidates="Model.Candidates"
                              Repositories="Model.Repositories"
                              OnAttach="subject => OnAttach.InvokeAsync(new GoalAttachRequest(goal.Id, subject))"
                              OnEdit="@(OnEditGoal.HasDelegate ? EventCallback.Factory.Create<GoalEditRequest>(this, request => OnEditGoal.InvokeAsync(request)) : default)"
                              OnDelete="@(OnDeleteGoal.HasDelegate ? EventCallback.Factory.Create(this, () => _deleting = goal) : default)"
                              OnDetach="@(OnDetach.HasDelegate ? EventCallback.Factory.Create<GoalSubject>(this, subject => OnDetach.InvokeAsync(new GoalDetachRequest(goal.Id, subject))) : default)"
                              OnQuickAdd="@(OnQuickAddTask.HasDelegate ? EventCallback.Factory.Create<string>(this, title => OnQuickAddTask.InvokeAsync(new GoalQuickAddRequest(goal.Id, title))) : default)"
                              EditError="@(goal.Id == _selected ? EditError : null)"
                              Busy="Busy"
                              TestId="@Part($"goal-{goal.Id}")" />
                }

                @if (Model.NoGoal.Count > 0)
                {
                    <section class="goals-board__no-goal" aria-labelledby="@($"{_id}-no-goal")" data-testid="@Part("no-goal")">
                        <div class="goals-board__no-goal-head">
                            <h3 class="goals-board__no-goal-title" id="@($"{_id}-no-goal")">No goal</h3>
                            <SearchBox Value="@_noGoalQuery"
                                       ValueChanged="value => _noGoalQuery = value"
                                       Placeholder="Search"
                                       AriaLabel="@NoGoalSearchLabel"
                                       DebounceMilliseconds="0"
                                       CssClass="goals-board__no-goal-search"
                                       TestId="@Part("no-goal-search")" />
                        </div>
                        @{ var noGoalShown = NoGoalShown; }
                        @if (noGoalShown.Count == 0)
                        {
                            <span class="goals-board__no-goal-none" role="status" data-testid="@Part("no-goal-none")">No matches</span>
                        }
                        @foreach (var item in noGoalShown)
                        {
                            <div class="goals-board__no-goal-row" data-kind="@GoalCard.KindLabel(item.Kind)">
                                <span class="goals-board__no-goal-item">
                                    @if (item.Number is { } number)
                                    {
                                        <span class="goals-board__number">#@number</span>@(" ")
                                    }
                                    @item.Title
                                </span>
                                <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                           Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                                           Disabled="@(Model.Goals.Count == 0)"
                                           title="@AttachTitle"
                                           OnClick="() => AttachFromNoGoalAsync(item)"
                                           TestId="@Part($"attach-{item.Subject.Key}")">Attach…</AppButton>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </section>
                }
            }
        </div>

        <StandUpPanel StandUp="Model.StandUp"
                      Iteration="Model.Iteration"
                      Busy="Busy"
                      OnMoveImpediment="request => OnMoveImpediment.InvokeAsync(request)"
                      OnEditImpedimentNote="@(OnEditImpedimentNote.HasDelegate ? EventCallback.Factory.Create<ImpedimentNoteRequest>(this, request => OnEditImpedimentNote.InvokeAsync(request)) : default)"
                      CssClass="goals-board__stand-up"
                      TestId="@Part("stand-up")" />
    </div>

    <ConfirmDialog Open="@(_deleting is not null)"
                   OpenChanged="open => { if (!open) _deleting = null; }"
                   Title="Delete this goal?"
                   Message="@DeleteMessage"
                   ConfirmText="Delete goal"
                   Destructive="true"
                   OnConfirm="ConfirmDeleteAsync"
                   OnCancel="() => _deleting = null"
                   TestId="@(Part("delete-confirm") ?? "goals-board-delete-confirm")"
                   ConfirmTestId="@(Part("delete-confirm-yes") ?? "goals-board-delete-confirm-yes")"
                   CancelTestId="@(Part("delete-confirm-no") ?? "goals-board-delete-confirm-no")" />
</div>

@code {
    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<GoalsIteration> Iterations =
        [GoalsIteration.Day, GoalsIteration.Week, GoalsIteration.TwoWeeks, GoalsIteration.Month];

    /// <summary>The No goal search's accessible name.</summary>
    private const string NoGoalSearchLabel = "Search work with no goal";

    private readonly string _id = "goals-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
    private string _noGoalQuery = string.Empty;
    private string? _selected;
    private string? _selectedParameter;
    private bool _initialised;
    private bool _announce;
    private GoalCardModel? _deleting;
    private bool _focusNewGoal;
    private readonly string _newGoalId = "goals-new-goal-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public GoalsBoardModel Model { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The goal to open; null opens the first when the board first draws.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? SelectedGoalId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A goal was opened, or folded to none — including the first goal the board
    /// opens on its own.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string?> SelectedGoalIdChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The iteration switch was moved.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalsIteration> IterationChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>New goal was pressed: the host opens <see cref="GoalCreateDialog"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnNewGoal { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Refresh was pressed: the host reads the view again.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnRefresh { get; set; }

    /// <summary>An item was picked to attach to a goal, from a goal's search or No goal.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalAttachRequest> OnAttach { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A No goal row's Attach… was pressed with no goal open: the host opens the
    /// GoalPicker for that work.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalSubject> OnPickGoal { get; set; }

    /// <summary>An impediment's state was picked.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<ImpedimentMoveRequest> OnMoveImpediment { get; set; }

    /// <summary>An impediment's note was written; without a listener the notes are text.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<ImpedimentNoteRequest> OnEditImpedimentNote { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A field of the open goal changed. Without a listener no goal is editable.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalEditRequest> OnEditGoal { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A goal's deletion was confirmed: its id. Without a listener there is no
    /// Delete goal….</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnDeleteGoal { get; set; }

    /// <summary>An item's Detach was pressed on a goal's row. Without a listener no row has one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalDetachRequest> OnDetach { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A goal's "New task" row was picked: the goal and the title typed. Without a
    /// listener no goal offers the row.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalQuickAddRequest> OnQuickAddTask { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A goal was moved — dragged by its grip, or Move up / Move down: the goal and
    /// its new place. Without a listener no goal can be moved.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalMoveRequest> OnMoveGoal { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Why the open goal's last edit was refused, in the module's words; shown in
    /// that goal, under its fields.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? EditError { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A refusal to show above the board, in the module's words.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Error { get; set; }

    /// <summary>While the host reads or writes: the switch, Refresh and the pickers wait.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Busy { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Lands on the board; its parts take it as a prefix.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; } = "goals-board";

    /// <summary>The empty state's test id.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string EmptyTestId { get; set; } = "goals-view-empty";

    private string ClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? "goals-board" : $"goals-board {CssClass}";

    private bool IsEmpty => Model.Goals.Count == 0 && Model.NoGoal.Count == 0;

    /// <summary>The No goal rows the search keeps, by the attach search's rule; every row
    /// for a blank query.</summary>
    private List<GoalsItem> NoGoalShown => [.. Model.NoGoal.Where(item => GoalCard.IsMatch(item, _noGoalQuery))];

    private GoalCardModel? Selected => Model.Goals.FirstOrDefault(goal => goal.Id == _selected);

    private string AttachTitle => Selected is { } goal
        ? $"Attach to {goal.Title}"
        : Model.Goals.Count == 0 ? "Set a goal first" : "Attach to a goal";

    private string? Part(string part) => TestId is null ? null : $"{TestId}-{part}";

    // --- The person's order ------------------------------------------------------

    private bool CanMoveGoals => OnMoveGoal.HasDelegate;

    /// <summary>The order drawn at once after a move, by goal id, until the host's next
    /// reading — a new <see cref="Model"/> — says what was stored.</summary>
    private List<string>? _placed;
    private GoalsBoardModel? _modelSeen;
    private string? _moveAnnouncement;

    /// <summary>The goal held in a pointer drag, and the goal it is over.</summary>
    private string? _dragging;
    private string? _over;
    private DotNetObjectReference<GoalsBoard>? _dragSelf;

    /// <summary>The goals in the order drawn: the model's, or the one a move drew at once.</summary>
    private List<GoalCardModel> Placed
    {
        get
        {
            if (_placed is null) return [.. Model.Goals];

            var byId = Model.Goals.ToDictionary(goal => goal.Id, StringComparer.Ordinal);
            return
            [
                .. _placed.Where(byId.ContainsKey).Select(id => byId[id]),
                .. Model.Goals.Where(goal => !_placed.Contains(goal.Id, StringComparer.Ordinal))
            ];
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The goals as shown: <see cref="Placed"/>, with a goal held in a drag drawn
    /// in the place it would land — the place of the goal it is over.</summary>
    private List<GoalCardModel> Shown =>
        _dragging is { } dragging && _over is { } over
            ? [.. new global::Backlog.UI.Components.Tasks.TaskMove(dragging, over).ApplyTo(Placed, goal => goal.Id)]
            : Placed;

    private Task MoveByAsync(string goalId, int delta)
    {
        var order = Placed;
        var from = order.FindIndex(goal => goal.Id == goalId);
        return from < 0 ? Task.CompletedTask : PlaceAsync(goalId, from + delta);
    }

    /// <summary>Draws the goal at <paramref name="to"/> at once, says where it went, and hands
    /// the move to the host; a refusal shows in <see cref="Error"/>, and the host's reading
    /// after it puts the stored order back.</summary>
    private async Task PlaceAsync(string goalId, int to)
    {
        var order = Placed;
        var from = order.FindIndex(goal => goal.Id == goalId);
        if (from < 0 || to < 0 || to >= order.Count || from == to) return;

        var goal = order[from];
        order.RemoveAt(from);
        order.Insert(to, goal);
        _placed = [.. order.Select(g => g.Id)];
        _moveAnnouncement = $"Moved {goal.Title} to position {to + 1} of {order.Count}.";

        await OnMoveGoal.InvokeAsync(new GoalMoveRequest(goalId, to));
    }

    /// <summary>A goal's grip was pressed and moved far enough to be a drag — the shared
    /// pointer reorder in components.js (<c>backlogListReorder</c>) owns the gesture, since a
    /// native drag is aborted in the desktop head's WebView2.</summary>
    [JSInvokable]
    public void PointerDragStart(string id)
    {
        if (!CanMoveGoals || Busy || Model.Goals.All(goal => goal.Id != id)) return;

        _dragging = id;
        _over = null;
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    /// <summary>The goal the pointer is over; the held goal is drawn in its place. The held
    /// goal's own id, or null for the gap between two cards, is no new target: the held goal
    /// now sits under the pointer, so taking either as one would put the order back and bring
    /// the target under the pointer again, frame after frame — the last target stands, as
    /// <c>TaskListView.DragOver</c> keeps it, and Escape is the way out.</summary>
    [JSInvokable]
    public void PointerDragOver(string? id)
    {
        if (_dragging is not { } dragging || id is null || string.Equals(id, dragging, StringComparison.Ordinal)) return;

        _over = id;
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    /// <summary>The pointer was released: the held goal takes the place of the last goal it
    /// was over, as the board was already showing. Never over another goal, nothing moves.</summary>
    [JSInvokable]
    public async Task PointerDragEnd()
    {
        var (dragging, over) = (_dragging, _over);
        _dragging = null;
        _over = null;

        if (dragging is not null && over is not null && dragging != over)
        {
            var to = Placed.FindIndex(goal => goal.Id == over);
            if (to >= 0) await PlaceAsync(dragging, to);
        }

        StateHasChanged();
    }

    /// <summary>The drag was taken away — Escape, a cancelled pointer, the window losing
    /// focus: the goal goes back where it was.</summary>
    [JSInvokable]
    public void PointerDragCancel()
    {
        _dragging = null;
        _over = null;
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        if (_dragSelf is null) return;

        try
        {
            await Js.InvokeVoidAsync("backlogListReorder.unregister", _id);
        }
        catch (JSException)
        {
        }
        catch (JSDisconnectedException)
        {
        }

        _dragSelf.Dispose();
    }

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (!ReferenceEquals(Model, _modelSeen))
        {
            _modelSeen = Model;
            _placed = null;
        }

        if (SelectedGoalId != _selectedParameter)
        {
            _selectedParameter = SelectedGoalId;
            _selected = SelectedGoalId;
            _initialised = true;
        }

        if (!_initialised && Model.Goals.Count > 0)
        {
            _selected = Model.Goals[0].Id;
            _initialised = true;
            _announce = true;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The first goal opened on the board's own say: a host bound to the selection
    /// is told, so it never believes no goal is open.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (CanMoveGoals && _dragSelf is null)
        {
            _dragSelf = DotNetObjectReference.Create(this);

            try
            {
                await Js.InvokeVoidAsync("backlogListReorder.register", _id, _dragSelf);
            }
            catch (JSException)
            {
            }
        }

        if (_focusNewGoal)
        {
            // The deleted goal took Delete goal… with it: the focus waits on New goal.
            _focusNewGoal = false;
            await global::Backlog.UI.Components.Tasks.QuickEditField.FocusAsync(Js, _newGoalId, select: false);
        }

        if (!_announce) return;

        _announce = false;
        await SelectedGoalIdChanged.InvokeAsync(_selected);
    }

    private async Task ToggleAsync(string goalId)
    {
        _selected = _selected == goalId ? null : goalId;
        await SelectedGoalIdChanged.InvokeAsync(_selected);
    }

    private Task AttachFromNoGoalAsync(GoalsItem item) =>
        Selected is { } goal
            ? OnAttach.InvokeAsync(new GoalAttachRequest(goal.Id, item.Subject))
            : OnPickGoal.InvokeAsync(item.Subject);

    private string DeleteMessage => _deleting is { } goal
        ? $"{goal.Title} is deleted. The plans, tasks and pull requests it holds stay as they are and belong to no goal."
        : string.Empty;

    private async Task ConfirmDeleteAsync()
    {
        if (_deleting is not { } goal) return;

        // The dialog stays open, Confirm busy, until the host has answered; a refusal
        // leaves the goal open where the person acted.
        await OnDeleteGoal.InvokeAsync(goal.Id);
        await Task.Yield();
        _deleting = null;
        if (Model.Goals.Any(g => g.Id == goal.Id) && Error is not null) return;

        _focusNewGoal = true;
        if (_selected == goal.Id)
        {
            _selected = null;
            await SelectedGoalIdChanged.InvokeAsync(null);
        }
    }
}
